erences is RGC responses may arise due to faster response kinetics of the cones themselves (Cao et al., 2007; Baylor & Hodgkin, 1973; Ingram et al., 2016; Schneeweis & Schnapf, 1995), the relative contribution of photoreceptors and downstream retinal circuits are not well understood. Models of retina that can leverage the power of deep learning to model multiple ganglion cells simultaneously, together with biologically tractable components, could be used to dissect the relative contributions by different components. At least in our photoreceptor-CNN model, switching to rod photoreceptor substan-\ntially reduces (Fig. 5b) the lag and the response frequency that was observed in the conventional CNN model predictions at dim light level of 1 R*rod\u22121s\u22121(Fig. 5a)."
